ts\n\nIf you have any more questions or need further information, feel free to ask!', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}), HumanMessage(content='who are the famous faculties are associated with this course?', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}), AIMessage(content='### Distinguished Faculty in the MS in Cybersecurity Program at Walden University\n\n1. **Robert Duhainy**\n   - Core Faculty in the College of Management and Human Potential\n   - Holds a Doctor of Information Technology (DIT) degree\n   - Extensive experience in designing and implementing wireless and cellular networks, technology, and computer security\n   - Teaches courses in Data Communications and Computer Security online\n   - Involved in security-related research projects and training from various security agencies\n\n2. **Gary Griffith**\n   - Academic Coordinator in the College of Management and Human Potential\n   - Holds a Doctor of Business Administration (DBA) degree\n   - Over 30 years of experience in information systems and technology\n   - Taught courses in IT programs and worked on cybersecurity initiatives\n   - Worked with IBM and Ingersoll Rand on software development and project management\n\nThese faculty members bring diverse expertise and a passion for teaching to the Walden community, enhancing the learning experience for students in the MS in Cybersecurity program.\n\nIf you have any more questions or need further information, feel free to ask!', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={})]' for
