nt. Applicants must also meet one of the following criteria:\n\nYou are 21 years of age or older.\nYou are less than 21 years of age with at least 12 quarter credits.\nYou are an active member of the military or a veteran with documentation of service. Choose Your Concentration\nChoose from eight BS in Business Administration concentrations to focus on the career and future you want. Accounting,Finance,General Program,Healthcare Management,Human Resource Management,Management,Marketing,Small Business Management.  tuition and fees : Tuition Breakdown\nWe know cost is a major consideration when exploring online BS in Business Administration programs. That’s why Walden offers opportunities to reduce your tuition through:\n\nExperience-based credits\n\nSpecial tuition savings\n\nBelieve & Achieve Scholarship. General Program Concentration Course-Based Learning = Curriculum Component\tRequirements\tCost\tAmount\nTuition\t181 quarter credit hours\t$350 per quarter hour\t\n$63,350\n\nProgram Fee\tPer quarter\t$180\t\n$2,880\n\n$66,230**\n\nBELIEVE & ACHIEVE SCHOLARSHIP\n\nYOUR TUITION\t\n-$19,250\n\n$46,980*\n\n. Books and materials are not included and may cost up to an additional $5,500. Tempo Learning = Progress at Your Pace. Control Your Cost.\n\nWalden’s Tempo Learning® programs follow a subscription-based pricing format. Students are billed a flat-rate for each 3-month subscription term. All pricing is represented in U.S. dollars and is subject to change.', 'url': 'https://www.waldenu.edu/online-bachelors-programs/bs-in-business-administration', 'url_path': '/online-bachelors-programs/'}, {'doc_id': '1-1-chunk-1', 'source': 'walden_university', 'text': "More information for international applicants. Questions about the courses you will take? We believe you can achieve your goals and we are here to support you along your journey. Request information to learn more about scholarships and financial aid for those who apply and qualify. Walden offers tuition savings options that can make your goals more attainable. Discover savings opportunities by exploring our scholarships and grants, for those who apply and qualify. Time to completion varies by student, depending on individual progress and credits transferred, if applicable. Tuition and time to complete may be reduced if transfer credits are accepted, or if you receive grants, scholarships, or other tuition reductions. Walden may accept up to 20 transfer credits. For a personalized estimate of the number of your transfer credits that Walden would accept, call an Enrollment Specialist at844-529-2438. Books and materials are not included and may cost up to an additional $1,000 and $1,400. PROGRAM OUTCOMES Our online master's in data science program integrates core business, compliance, and management principles with the rigorous, hands-on training you need to excel in your field. Explore machine learning as you discover how to collect, analyze, and visualize an ever-growing volume of data from information systems. Learn to share insights with stakeholders to empower better decision-making. Work toward becoming the voice of data responsibility and the go-to data expert in your organization and beyond. Career Outlook Now more than ever, businesses need data scientists to help them interpret and leverage a growing volume of raw data. An online data science degree program can help provide you with the hands-on training and specialized technical knowledge necessary to fill this pressing need.", 'url': 'https://www.waldenu.edu/online-masters-programs/ms-in-data-science', 'url_path': '/online-masters-programs/ms-in-data-science'}, {'doc_id': '5-0-chunk-2', 'source': '', 'text': ' learning track offers support, tuition savings, and resources for those without previous college credit.Career Resources\n\nTake advantage of our Career Planning and Development Center for one-on-one guidance, networking events, essential job search tools, and more.Applying is Easy\n\nNo application fee, essay, or SAT or ACT score is required for admission. Bachelor’s Programs BS in Business Administration, BS in Communication.  An Accredited University\nQuality matters—especially when it comes to your education. Walden is accredited by The Higher Learning Commission and committed to maintaining the highest standards of excellence. Flexibility to Fit Your Schedule\nAt Walden, we are dedicated to offering education options designed to fit the needs of working professionals like you. That is why we offer a wide range of learning options, including a standard, course-based experience, and Tempo Learning®. COURSE BASED\nInstructor-led\nEngage in a course-by-course experience, where you progress on a predetermined schedule. This format allows you to learn alongside your peers, participating in weekly discussions and meeting established deadlines for assignments. Your cost is based on how many credits you need to complete your program.\n\nIdeal for students who are newer to online education and prefer structure, working with others, and having set deadlines.\n\nStarts on May 26\n\nRegister and pay by course.\n\nCourse lengths are predetermined, based on program.\n\nFaculty guide you through each course.\n\nScheduled due dates allow you make steady progress.', 'url': 'https://www.waldenu.edu/online-bachelors-programs', 'url_path': '/online-bachelors-programs/'}, {'doc_id': '1-3-chunk-1', 'source': 'walden_university', 'text': "is beneficial for students to have at least a foundational understanding before pursuing a master's degree in the field. That's because programming helps data scientists to process, analyze, and generate predictions from data. Python, R, and SQL are just a few of the programming languages used to tackle specific tasks. Sifting through and analyzing large datasets is a key part of the job, so the ability to understand one or more of these languages is essential. The fees structure of MS in Data Science program  (Type: financial): Financial/Tuition Information: Tuition - 45 quarter credit hours - $565 per quarter hour - $25,425 Program Fee - Per quarter - $180 - $900 - - - $26,325** Total Cost: $26,325**", 'url': 'https://www.waldenu.edu/online-masters-programs/ms-in-data-science', 'url_path': '/online-masters-programs/ms-in-data-science'}, {'doc_id': '3-1-chunk-1', 'source': 'walden_university', 'text': "Streamlined Admissions Process\nEarning your MS in Cybersecurity degree online is a big decision, which is why we’ve streamlined and simplified the admissions process. Start your journey with:\n\nNo application fee\n\nEasy credit transfer\n\nNo essay. Admission Criteria : Program Admission Considerations: A bachelor's degree or higher. Tuition Breakdown \nWalden offers tuition savings options that can make your goals more attainable. Discover savings opportunities by exploring our scholarships and grants, for those who apply and qualify.\n\nBelieve & Achieve Scholarship®\n\nWalden grants\n\nFederal and state grants   Curriculum Component\tRequirements\tCost\tAmount\nTuition\t45 quarter credit hours\t$565 per quarter hour\t\n$25,425\n\nProgram Fee\tPer quarter\t$180\t\n$900\n\n$26,325**\nBELIEVE & ACHIEVE SCHOLARSHIP\n\nYOUR TUITION\t\n-$5,650\n\n$20,675*\n\n. Books and materials are not included and may cost up to an additional $1,000 and $1,400.   **Tuition reflects the minimum time to completion. Time to completion varies by student, depending on individual progress and credits transferred, if applicable. Tuition and time to complete may be reduced if transfer credits are accepted, or if you receive grants, scholarships, or other tuition reductions. Walden may accept up to 20 transfer credits. For a personalized estimate of the number of your transfer credits that Walden would accept. PROGRAM OUTCOMES", 'url': 'https://www.waldenu.edu/online-masters-programs/ms-in-cybersecurity', 'url_path': '/online-masters-programs/'}, {'doc_id': '6-2-chunk-7', 'source': '', 'text': '350 per quarter hour\t\n$63,350\n\nProgram Fee\tPer quarter\t$180\t\n$2,880\n\n$66,230**\nBELIEVE & ACHIEVE SCHOLARSHIP\n\nYOUR TUITION\t-$19,250\n\n$46,980*. Choose Your Concentration\nChoose from three BS in Communication specializations to focus on the career and future you want. Healing, Hierarchy, Healthcare, and Wholeness. Organizational Society, Branding, and Global Citizenship. Possibilities, Problems, and the Human Condition. PROGRAM OUTCOMES\n\nMaster the Science of Strategic Communication\nIn our online bachelor’s degree program, you’ll explore the role and power of communication throughout all facets of human interaction. Coursework covers topics such as interpersonal communication, group communication, digital storytelling, and intercultural communication. Learn what it takes to create a personal identity, sell ideas to others, speak persuasively in public, and analyze messages from mass media. Build a highly transferable skill set that benefits you both in your personal life and in your career endeavors.\n\nCareer Outlook\nCommunication plays a central role in creating and sustaining interpersonal relationships, organizations, cultures, and global societies. In the age of digitization and automation, communicating clearly and making meaningful human connections has become even more important.', 'url': 'https://www.waldenu.edu/online-bachelors-programs/bs-in-communication', 'url_path': '/online-bachelors-programs/'}, {'doc_id': '4-2-chunk-1', 'source': 'walden_university', 'text': "Streamlined Admissions Process\nEarning your Online Master’s Degree in Criminal Justice is a big decision, which is why we’ve streamlined and simplified the admissions process. Start your journey with:\n\nNo application fee\n\nEasy credit transfer\n\nNo essay. Admission Criteria Program Admission Considerations: A bachelor's degree or higher.  Fees structure Curriculum Component\tRequirements\tCost\tAmount\nTuition\t48 total quarter credit hours\t$560 per quarter hour\t\n$26,880\n\nProgram Fee\tPer quarter\t$180\t\n$900\n\n$