2025-04-25 23:52:17,851 - walden_rag - INFO - Data from vectore DB: '[{'doc_id': '1-1-chunk-1', 'source': 'walden_university', 'text': "More information for international applicants. Questions about the courses you will take? We believe you can achieve your goals and we are here to support you along your journey. Request information to learn more about scholarships and financial aid for those who apply and qualify. Walden offers tuition savings options that can make your goals more attainable. Discover savings opportunities by exploring our scholarships and grants, for those who apply and qualify. Time to completion varies by student, depending on individual progress and credits transferred, if applicable. Tuition and time to complete may be reduced if transfer credits are accepted, or if you receive grants, scholarships, or other tuition reductions. Walden may accept up to 20 transfer credits. For a personalized estimate of the number of your transfer credits that Walden would accept, call an Enrollment Specialist at844-529-2438. Books and materials are not included and may cost up to an additional $1,000 and $1,400. PROGRAM OUTCOMES Our online master's in data science program integrates core business, compliance, and management principles with the rigorous, hands-on training you need to excel in your field. Explore machine learning as you discover how to collect, analyze, and visualize an ever-growing volume of data from information systems. Learn to share insights with stakeholders to empower better decision-making. Work toward becoming the voice of data responsibility and the go-to data expert in your organization and beyond. Career Outlook Now more than ever, businesses need data scientists to help them interpret and leverage a growing volume of raw data. An online data science degree program can help provide you with the hands-on training and specialized technical knowledge necessary to fill this pressing need.", 'url': 'https://www.waldenu.edu/online-masters-programs/ms-in-data-science', 'url_path': '/online-masters-programs/ms-in-data-science'}, {'doc_id': '5-0-chunk-1', 'source': '', 'text': 'Online Bachelor’s Programs\nDiscover online bachelor’s degree programs that can help advance your career .Turn Your Ambition Into Achievement With Walden Wayfinder™\nYour journey of change doesn’t have to be a solo mission. Follow Walden Wayfinder™, a guided, all-inclusive path that begins with your destination in mind. You won’t just earn your online bachelor’s degree; you’ll get a personalized, step-by-step road map to a thriving career. From exclusive tuition savings to integrated career planning from Day 1, Walden takes the guesswork out of preparing for your future. You bring your dreams and ambitions—we’ll show you the way forward. Program Variety\n\n.Transfer of Credit\n\nTransfer up to 75% of credits required for your degree program from past college courses, military service, or an associate degree.Walden Undergraduate Academy®\n\nThis dedicated online learning track offers support, tuition savings, and resources for those without previous college credit.Career Resources\n\nTake advantage of our Career Planning and Development Center for one-on-one guidance, networking events, essential job search tools, and more.Applying is Easy', 'url': 'https://www.waldenu.edu/online-bachelors-programs', 'url_path': '/online-bachelors-programs/'}, {'doc_id': '3-1-chunk-1', 'source': 'walden_university', 'text': "Streamlined Admissions Process\nEarning your MS in Cybersecurity degree online is a big decision, which is why we’ve streamlined and simplified the admissions process. Start your journey with:\n\nNo application fee\n\nEasy credit transfer\n\nNo essay. Admission Criteria : Program Admission Considerations: A bachelor's degree or higher. Tuition Breakdown \nWalden offers tuition savings options that can make your goals more attainable. Discover savings opportunities by exploring our scholarships and grants, for those who apply and qualify.\n\nBelieve & Achieve Scholarship®\n\nWalden grants\n\nFederal and state grants   Curriculum Component\tRequirements\tCost\tAmount\nTuition\t45 quarter credit hours\t$565 per quarter hour\t\n$25,425\n\nProgram Fee\tPer quarter\t$180\t\n$900\n\n$26,325**\nBELIEVE & ACHIEVE SCHOLARSHIP\n\nYOUR TUITION\t\n-$5,650\n\n$20,675*\n\n. Books and materials are not included and may cost up to an additional $1,000 and $1,400.   **Tuition reflects the minimum time to completion. Time to completion varies by student, depending on individual progress and credits transferred, if applicable. Tuition and time to complete may be reduced if transfer credits are accepted, or if you receive grants, scholarships, or other tuition reductions. Walden may accept up to 20 transfer credits. For a personalized estimate of the number of your transfer credits that Walden would accept. PROGRAM OUTCOMES", 'url': 'https://www.waldenu.edu/online-masters-programs/ms-in-cybersecurity', 'url_path': '/online-masters-programs/'}, {'doc_id': '6-0-chunk-3', 'source': '', 'text': ' the admissions process. Start your journey with:\n\nNo application fee\n\nEasy credit transfer\n\nNo essay.  Admission Criteria = Admission is considered for adult students who hold a high school diploma or its equivalent. Applicants must also meet one of the following criteria:\n\nYou are 21 years of age or older.\nYou are less than 21 years of age with at least 12 quarter credits.\nYou are an active member of the military or a veteran with documentation of service. Choose Your Concentration\nChoose from eight BS in Business Administration concentrations to focus on the career and future you want. Accounting,Finance,General Program,Healthcare Management,Human Resource Management,Management,Marketing,Small Business Management.  tuition and fees : Tuition Breakdown\nWe know cost is a major consideration when exploring online BS in Business Administration programs. That’s why Walden offers opportunities to reduce your tuition through:\n\nExperience-based credits\n\nSpecial tuition savings\n\nBelieve & Achieve Scholarship. General Program Concentration Course-Based Learning = Curriculum Component\tRequirements\tCost\tAmount\nTuition\t181 quarter credit hours\t$350 per quarter hour\t\n$63,350\n\nProgram Fee\tPer quarter\t$180\t\n$2,880\n\n$66,230**\n\nBELIEVE & ACHIEVE SCHOLARSHIP\n\nYOUR TUITION\t\n-$19,250\n\n$46,980*\n\n. Books and materials are not included and may cost up to an additional $5,500. Tempo Learning = Progress at Your Pace. Control Your Cost.\n\nWalden’s Tempo Learning® programs follow a subscription-based pricing format. Students are billed a flat-rate for each 3-month subscription term. All pricing is represented in U.S. dollars and is subject to change.', 'url': 'https://www.waldenu.edu/online-bachelors-programs/bs-in-business-administration', 'url_path': '/online-bachelors-programs/'}, {'doc_id': '6-2-chunk-4', 'source': '', 'text': '–25 credits, depending on concentration)\nElective courses (55–80 credits, depending on concentration)\nCapstone course (5 credits)\nCurriculum\nGeneral Education Courses (46 credits)\nSee the General Education section of this Walden University Catalog.\n\nNote: A minimum of 60 quarter credits must be completed at the 3000 or 4000 level in order to meet program requirements. In some cases, this means that students will need to select 3000 or 4000 level courses as either general education or elective options. Students should consult their student success advisor if they have questions about individual program requirements.', 'url': 'https://www.waldenu.edu/online-bachelors-programs/bs-in-communication', 'url_path': '/online-bachelors-programs/'}, {'doc_id': '6-1-chunk-2', 'source': '', 'text': '15 credits, depending on concentration)\nElective courses (60–75 credits, depending on concentration) \nCapstone course (5 credits)\nCurriculum\n\nGeneral Education Courses (46 credits)\nSee the General Education section of this Walden University Catalog.\n\nNote: A minimum of 60 quarter credits must be completed at the 3000 or 4000 level in order to meet program requirements. In some cases, this means that students will need to select 3000 or 4000 level courses as either general education or elective options. Students should consult their student success advisor if they have questions about individual program requirements.', 'url': 'https://academics.waldenu.edu/catalog/management-human-potential/undergraduate/bachelor-science-business-administration', 'url_path': '/online-bachelors-programs/'}, {'doc_id': '5-0-chunk-2', 'source': '', 'text': ' learning track offers support, tuition savings, and resources for those without previous college credit.Career Resources\n\nTake advantage of our Career Planning and Development Center for one-on-one guidance, networking events, essential job search tools, and more.Applying is Easy\n\nNo application fee, essay, or SAT or ACT score is required for admission. Bachelor’s Programs BS in Business Administration, BS in Communication.  An Accredited University\nQuality matters—especially when it comes to your education. Walden is accredited by The Higher Learning Commission and committed to maintaining the highest standards of excellence. Flexibility to Fit Your Schedule\nAt Walden, we are dedicated to offering education options designed to fit the needs of working professionals like you. That is why we offer a wide range of learning options, including a standard, course-based experience, and Tempo Learning®. COURSE BASED\nInstructor-led\nEngage in a course-by-course experience, where you progress on a predetermined schedule. This format allows you to learn alongside your peers, participating in weekly discussions and meeting established deadlines for assignments. Your cost is based on how many credits you need to complete your program.\n\nIdeal for students who are newer to online education and prefer structure, working with others, and having set deadlines.\n\nStarts on May 26\n\nRegister and pay by course.\n\nCourse lengths are predetermined, based on program.\n\nFaculty guide you through each course.\n\nScheduled due dates allow you make steady progress.', 'url': 'https://www.waldenu.edu/online-bachelors-programs', 'url_path': '/online-bachelors-programs/'}, {'doc_id': '6-1-chunk-5', 'source': '', 'text': " Students progress through the Tempo Learning® model by successfully passing competency assessments. A student must successfully achieve or master all competency assessments to graduate from the program.\n\nStudents earn the same Walden degree whether they choose the course-based or the competency-based modality.\n\nDegree Requirements\n181 total quarter credit hours\nGeneral Education courses (45 credits)\nCore competencies (61 credits) or\nAIM core competencies (66 credits)\nElective courses (70 credits) or\nAIM elective courses (65 credits)\nCapstone competency (5 credits)\n BS in Business Administration (General Program)\n Accelerate Into Master's\nNote on Curriculum\nIn an effort to ensure competencies are kept up to date and relevant to meet the learning outcomes of the program, the number and subject matter of individual competencies needed to satisfy program course requirements may change. However, program outcomes and the number and subject matter of courses will not be impacted. As a result, the required competencies listed in a student’s individual learning plan may differ from what is currently listed in the catalog. Faculty of this program Shannon Lynch\nContributing Faculty. College of Management and Technology\nB.S. Business Administration (BSBA).  Dr. Shannon Lynch is a Contributing Faculty Member in the College of Management & Human Potential. Dr. Lynch has served in various capacities during her time at Walden which has spanned over 21 years. She has experience and interest in Human Resources as a certified HR Professional through SHRM. She was also a school administrator for a number of years and has the unique background of both an educator and a human resource practitioner.\n\nCourses Taught\nHRMG 4201 - Strategic Human Resource Management\n\nHRMG 3001 - Human Resource Management", 'url': 'https://academics.waldenu.edu/catalog/management-human-potential/undergraduate/bachelor-science-business-administration', 'url_path': '/online-bachelors-programs/'}, {'doc_id': '6-2-chunk-6', 'source': '', 'text': '4001 - Intercultural Communication* (5 credits)\nStudents may take this as a non-degree course.\nConcentration Courses (0–25 credits)\nThese courses are dependent upon the particular concentration. Please see the course list on each concentration page.\n\nGeneral Program\n Concentration in Healing, Hierarchy, Healthcare, and Wholeness\n Concentration in Organizational Society, Branding, and Global Citizenship\n Concentration in Possibilities, Problems, and the Human Condition\nElectives (55–80 credits)\nElectives are dependent upon the particular concentration. Please see the elective requirements on each concentration page.\n\nCapstone Course (5 credits)\nCOMM 4901 - Communication Capstone (5 credits). Streamlined Admissions Process\nEarning your BS in Communication degree online is a bold step forward on your professional path. Walden makes it easier with our streamlined admissions process that includes:\n\nNo application fee\n\nEasy credit transfer\n\nNo essay. Admission Criteria. Admission is considered for adult students who hold a high school diploma or its equivalent. Applicants must also meet one of the following criteria:\n\nYou are 21 years of age or older.\nYou are less than 21 years of age with at least 12 quarter credits.\nYou are an active member of the military or a veteran with documentation of service. the fees structure Curriculum Component\tRequirements\tCost\tAmount\nTuition\t181 quarter credit hours\t$350 per quarter hour\t\n$63,350\n\nProgram Fee\tPer quarter\t$180\t\n$2,880\n\n$66,230**\nBELIEVE & ACHIEVE SCHOLARSHIP\n\nYOUR TUITION\t-$19,250', 'url': 'https://www.waldenu.edu/online-bachelors-programs/bs-in-communication', 'url_path': '/online-bachelors-programs/'}, {'doc_id': '6-2-chunk-1', 'source': '', 'text': 'Online BS in Communication\nMaster practical, applicable communication skills you can use in any setting—from professional endeavors to everyday interactions. why walden Learn to Better Connect, Engage, and Motivate With a BS in Communication\nNo matter where life takes you, your success often depends on being able to communicate effectively. Walden’s BS in Communication program focuses on the practical tools you need to make your voice heard and your message understood. First, build a strong communication foundation that can enhance your personal and professional growth. Then, apply these principles to a program concentration that reflects your specific area of interest.\n\nAn online communication degree prepares students to write, share, and present ideas and messaging impactfully to their audience. BUILD ACTIONABLE SKILLS\n\nApply theory to learn practical skills and concepts you can begin using immediately—at work and in your daily life. WALDEN UNDERGRADUATE ACADEMY®\n\nGet dedicated support, tuition savings,1 and resources if you have no prior college credits. Learn with other first-time college students.\n\nPERSONALIZE YOUR LEARNING\n\nChoose our General Program or one of three concentrations to build skills in an area you’re passionate about. Program Details\n\nTake a Closer Look\nLearn more about Walden’s BS in Communication program, from our streamlined admissions requirements to our rigorous curriculum. Curriculum – General Program\nDegree Completion Requirements', 'url': 'https://www.waldenu.edu/online-bachelors-programs/bs-in-communication', 'url_path': '/online-bachelors-programs/'}]' >>>>>>>>>>>>>>
