2025-04-25 23:53:16,694 - walden_rag - INFO - Data from vectore DB: '[{'doc_id': '3-2-chunk-3', 'source': 'walden_university', 'text': "uhainy, B. (2021). Ways to Bloom Where You’re Planted. Information Security Professional ISC2\n\nPresentations\nDUHAINY, B. (2022). Cybersecurity Attacks and Countermeasures . FBI Citizens Academy\n\nDuhainy, B. (2022). Infrastructure Security. FBI Citizens Academy Duhainy, B. (2020). Cybersecurity in the age of AI, Automation and GDPR. Walden University. Gary Griffith\nAcademic Coordinator  \nCollege of Management and Human Potential\nDoctor of Business Administration (DBA)   Dr. Gary Griffith started teaching as a contributing faculty for Walden University in the Master of Science in Information Systems Management program in 2011. In 2012 I accepted a core faculty position in the Master of Science in Information Technology program. Since starting my career at Walden University I have taught 16 different courses in BSIT, MISM, MSIT and DIT programs. Most of the courses I teach are in Walden University's Health Informatics, Software Engineering, and Cyber Security Master's degree programs. I performed the research which enabled Walden University to be designated as an NSA Center in Academic Excellence in Cyber Defense in 2014. I was part of a team working closely with leadership to design and implement new master’s degree specialization in Big Data Analytics. Recently I have started helping students in the DIT program where I am the dissertation chair and committee member.\nPrior to coming to Walden University, I worked in the field of information systems and technology for over 30 years.", 'url': 'https://www.waldenu.edu/online-masters-programs/ms-in-cybersecurity', 'url_path': '/online-masters-programs/'}, {'doc_id': '6-1-chunk-5', 'source': '', 'text': " Students progress through the Tempo Learning® model by successfully passing competency assessments. A student must successfully achieve or master all competency assessments to graduate from the program.\n\nStudents earn the same Walden degree whether they choose the course-based or the competency-based modality.\n\nDegree Requirements\n181 total quarter credit hours\nGeneral Education courses (45 credits)\nCore competencies (61 credits) or\nAIM core competencies (66 credits)\nElective courses (70 credits) or\nAIM elective courses (65 credits)\nCapstone competency (5 credits)\n BS in Business Administration (General Program)\n Accelerate Into Master's\nNote on Curriculum\nIn an effort to ensure competencies are kept up to date and relevant to meet the learning outcomes of the program, the number and subject matter of individual competencies needed to satisfy program course requirements may change. However, program outcomes and the number and subject matter of courses will not be impacted. As a result, the required competencies listed in a student’s individual learning plan may differ from what is currently listed in the catalog. Faculty of this program Shannon Lynch\nContributing Faculty. College of Management and Technology\nB.S. Business Administration (BSBA).  Dr. Shannon Lynch is a Contributing Faculty Member in the College of Management & Human Potential. Dr. Lynch has served in various capacities during her time at Walden which has spanned over 21 years. She has experience and interest in Human Resources as a certified HR Professional through SHRM. She was also a school administrator for a number of years and has the unique background of both an educator and a human resource practitioner.\n\nCourses Taught\nHRMG 4201 - Strategic Human Resource Management\n\nHRMG 3001 - Human Resource Management", 'url': 'https://academics.waldenu.edu/catalog/management-human-potential/undergraduate/bachelor-science-business-administration', 'url_path': '/online-bachelors-programs/'}, {'doc_id': '6-0-chunk-3', 'source': '', 'text': ' the admissions process. Start your journey with:\n\nNo application fee\n\nEasy credit transfer\n\nNo essay.  Admission Criteria = Admission is considered for adult students who hold a high school diploma or its equivalent. Applicants must also meet one of the following criteria:\n\nYou are 21 years of age or older.\nYou are less than 21 years of age with at least 12 quarter credits.\nYou are an active member of the military or a veteran with documentation of service. Choose Your Concentration\nChoose from eight BS in Business Administration concentrations to focus on the career and future you want. Accounting,Finance,General Program,Healthcare Management,Human Resource Management,Management,Marketing,Small Business Management.  tuition and fees : Tuition Breakdown\nWe know cost is a major consideration when exploring online BS in Business Administration programs. That’s why Walden offers opportunities to reduce your tuition through:\n\nExperience-based credits\n\nSpecial tuition savings\n\nBelieve & Achieve Scholarship. General Program Concentration Course-Based Learning = Curriculum Component\tRequirements\tCost\tAmount\nTuition\t181 quarter credit hours\t$350 per quarter hour\t\n$63,350\n\nProgram Fee\tPer quarter\t$180\t\n$2,880\n\n$66,230**\n\nBELIEVE & ACHIEVE SCHOLARSHIP\n\nYOUR TUITION\t\n-$19,250\n\n$46,980*\n\n. Books and materials are not included and may cost up to an additional $5,500. Tempo Learning = Progress at Your Pace. Control Your Cost.\n\nWalden’s Tempo Learning® programs follow a subscription-based pricing format. Students are billed a flat-rate for each 3-month subscription term. All pricing is represented in U.S. dollars and is subject to change.', 'url': 'https://www.waldenu.edu/online-bachelors-programs/bs-in-business-administration', 'url_path': '/online-bachelors-programs/'}, {'doc_id': '6-0-chunk-1', 'source': '', 'text': "Bachelor’s in Business Administration\nGain key business competencies, build your confidence, and ignite your growth in our BS in Business Administration online program. Why walden Build a Versatile Skill Set With a BS in Business Administration Online \nAre you looking to grow in your organization—or expand your possibilities? Walden’s BS in Business Administration online program is the smarter, more efficient way to launch your future in business.\n\nThis bachelor’s in business administration online program can help you develop professional confidence as well as essential hard and soft skills. You’ll engage in digital simulations of true-to-life business scenarios, allowing you to learn to navigate real challenges happening in today’s workplaces. BUILD SOFT SKILLS\nWalden’s program focuses on the eight “soft skills” that can help position you for success in the workplace. These include gaining a growth mindset, developing your emotional intelligence, and building skills in evidence- based decision-making. LEARN BY DOING\n\nOur capstone is a competitive, team-based business simulation exercise that immerses you in a realistic business challenge. BE SUPPORTED AT EACH STEP\n\nWith proactive student support services and engaged faculty, you’re never alone in your program. We’re always here for you. ABILITY TO SAVE TIME AND MONEY\n\nYou could transfer up to 75% of your required credits into Walden's BS in Business Administration online program. Program Details\n\nTake a Closer Look\nDiscover what it’s like to earn your bachelor’s in business administration online at Walden, from our transfer-of-credit policy to our engaging curriculum.Standard Program  = 181\nQUARTER CREDITS\n\n48 Months\nTIME TO COMPLETE", 'url': 'https://www.waldenu.edu/online-bachelors-programs/bs-in-business-administration', 'url_path': '/online-bachelors-programs/'}, {'doc_id': '5-0-chunk-2', 'source': '', 'text': ' learning track offers support, tuition savings, and resources for those without previous college credit.Career Resources\n\nTake advantage of our Career Planning and Development Center for one-on-one guidance, networking events, essential job search tools, and more.Applying is Easy\n\nNo application fee, essay, or SAT or ACT score is required for admission. Bachelor’s Programs BS in Business Administration, BS in Communication.  An Accredited University\nQuality matters—especially when it comes to your education. Walden is accredited by The Higher Learning Commission and committed to maintaining the highest standards of excellence. Flexibility to Fit Your Schedule\nAt Walden, we are dedicated to offering education options designed to fit the needs of working professionals like you. That is why we offer a wide range of learning options, including a standard, course-based experience, and Tempo Learning®. COURSE BASED\nInstructor-led\nEngage in a course-by-course experience, where you progress on a predetermined schedule. This format allows you to learn alongside your peers, participating in weekly discussions and meeting established deadlines for assignments. Your cost is based on how many credits you need to complete your program.\n\nIdeal for students who are newer to online education and prefer structure, working with others, and having set deadlines.\n\nStarts on May 26\n\nRegister and pay by course.\n\nCourse lengths are predetermined, based on program.\n\nFaculty guide you through each course.\n\nScheduled due dates allow you make steady progress.', 'url': 'https://www.waldenu.edu/online-bachelors-programs', 'url_path': '/online-bachelors-programs/'}, {'doc_id': '6-1-chunk-7', 'source': '', 'text': ' Limits , Volunteer - Austin\n\nAwards / Honors\nOutstanding Principal Award, Eanes ISD, 2001\n\nPublications\nLynch, S. (2011). Answering the Critics of Online Education. www.NAS.org\n\nPresentations\nLynch, S. (2016). Special Education in the Public School. Austin Community College. Next faculty is Harry Kemp\nContributing Faculty \nCollege of Management and Technology\nB.S. Business Administration (BSBA)\nDr. Harry Kemp is a Walden University professor and SCORE mentor with extensive expertise in business management. As a former firefighter and author of "How Small Businesses Survived Natural Disasters in Northeastern Florida," Dr. Kemp has valuable insight into disaster management and preparedness for small businesses. He has also been recognized as a Frank Dilley Award winner for his significant contributions to Walden University\'s mission.\nDr. Kemp is an accredited Financial Analyst (AFA) designation from the Global Academy of Finance and Management (GAFM), Dr. Kemp brings specialized knowledge and expertise in financial analysis to his work as a professor and mentor. His multifaceted background and experience as a SCORE mentor make him a valuable resource for entrepreneurs and small business owners seeking to grow and overcome challenges. Dr. Kemp\'s dedication to education, research, and professional development make him a distinguished professional in his field.\n\nEducation\nDBA, Walden University\n\nMBA, Jacksonville University\n\nBS, Edward Waters University\n\nAS, Florida State College at Jacksonville\n\nAA, Florida State College at Jacksonville\n\nPresentations\nKemp, H. A. (2019). The Survival of Small Businesses in Northeastern Florida After A Natural Disaster . Newport Restoration Foundation (NRF)', 'url': 'https://academics.waldenu.edu/catalog/management-human-potential/undergraduate/bachelor-science-business-administration', 'url_path': '/online-bachelors-programs/'}, {'doc_id': '6-0-chunk-6', 'source': '', 'text': ' sales team.\n\nExpected growth: 4%3\n\nEstimated annual wage: $63,700–$196,7003. Learning Outcomes\nAs a graduate of Walden’s BS in Business Administration online program, you’ll be prepared to:\n\nDemonstrate proficiency in the fundamental business principles and practices that enable firms to operate in both domestic and global environments.\n\nEmploy critical thinking and analysis skills to solve business problems in a real-world context.\n\nAnalyze ethical issues that impact business decisions from economic, political, legal, and social perspectives.\n\nDescribe the ways in which diversity influences a company’s ability to achieve its goals.\n\nEvaluate the application of technology as a strategy for competitive advantage in business.\n\nConduct basic research using scholarly sources to acquire new knowledge in the business domain.', 'url': 'https://www.waldenu.edu/online-bachelors-programs/bs-in-business-administration', 'url_path': '/online-bachelors-programs/'}, {'doc_id': '6-1-chunk-4', 'source': '', 'text': '.\nSTAT 2002 - Business Statistics* (5 credits)\nStudents may take this as a non-degree course.\nElectives (60–75 credits)\nElectives are dependent upon the particular concentration. Please see the elective requirements on each concentration page.\n\nConcentration Courses (0–15 credits)\nThese courses are dependent upon the particular concentration. Please see the course list on each concentration page.\n\nBS in Business Administration (General Program)\n Concentration in Accounting\n Concentration in Data Science (no longer accepting new students)\n Concentration in Finance\n Concentration in Healthcare Management\n Concentration in Human Resource Management\n Concentration in Information Systems (no longer accepting new students)\n Concentration in Management\n Concentration in Marketing\n Concentration in Small Business Management\nCapstone Course (5 credits)\nBUSI 4900 - Capstone: Strategic Business Management (5 credits)\nTempo Learning® Curriculum\nTempo Learning® is Walden’s competency-based education modality, an alternative way of earning a Walden degree offered for some Walden programs. Instead of courses, the Walden Tempo Learning® program is comprised of competencies and rigorous assessments. Students progress through the Tempo Learning® model by successfully passing competency assessments. A student must successfully achieve or master all competency assessments to graduate from the program.\n\nStudents earn the same Walden degree whether they choose the course-based or the competency-based modality.', 'url': 'https://academics.waldenu.edu/catalog/management-human-potential/undergraduate/bachelor-science-business-administration', 'url_path': '/online-bachelors-programs/'}, {'doc_id': '6-0-chunk-5', 'source': '', 'text': ' self-motivated learner with strong time management skills.\nStarts on May 05, 2025\n\n$15,000\nComplete in 16 months*\n\n3-month subscription pricing\n\nFlexible schedule\n\nPersonal Academic Coach.  PROGRAM OUTCOMES\n\nIgnite Your Growth\nYou don’t just want a job; you want a career. Earning your BS in Business Administration from Walden can provide you with the credibility, skills, and self-confidence it takes to achieve your goals. Our online bachelor’s in business administration is a practical program focused on the issues and challenges confronting today’s workplaces, whether in management or marketing. Benefit from a clear roadmap and a definitive structure along with all the tools and support you need to excel.\n\nCareer Opportunities\nA BS in Business Administration degree can help prepare you for a variety of professional paths in a range of organizations and fields.\n\nSteady Job Growth\n\nAdministrative Services Manager\n\nAdministrative managers plan and direct activities that help organizations run efficiently.\n\nExpected growth: 6%1\n\nEstimated annual wage: $62,470–$140,8701\n\nBe a Changemaker\nManagement Analyst\n\nRecommend ways to improve an organization’s efficiency; offer strategies to increase profitability.\n\nExpected growth: 10%2\n\nEstimated annual wage: $57,840–$130,8002\n\nOversee Sales Initiatives\n\nSALES Manager\n\nLead sales teams, set sales goals, analyze data, and develop training programs for sales team.\n\nExpected growth: 4%3\n\nEstimated annual wage: $63,700–$196,7003. Learning Outcomes\nAs a graduate of Walden’s BS in Business Administration online program, you’ll be prepared to:', 'url': 'https://www.waldenu.edu/online-bachelors-programs/bs-in-business-administration', 'url_path': '/online-bachelors-programs/'}, {'doc_id': '6-0-chunk-4', 'source': '', 'text': ' Pace. Control Your Cost.\n\nWalden’s Tempo Learning® programs follow a subscription-based pricing format. Students are billed a flat-rate for each 3-month subscription term. All pricing is represented in U.S. dollars and is subject to change.\n\nProgram\tSubscription Period Tuition\tSubscription Period program Fee\tSubscription Period Time Frame\nBS in Business Administration\t$2,650\t$175\t3-month subscription period\nYou may be able to complete your BS in Business Administration degree in 16 months for under $15,000.*\nEffective March 3, 2025\n\nProgram\tSubscription Period Tuition\tSubscription Period PROGRAM Fee\tSubscription Period Time Frame\nBS in Business Administration\t$2,750\t$180\t3-month subscription period\nYou may be able to complete your BS in Business Administration degree in 16 months for under $15,000.*.  Go at Your Own Pace\nYou have a unique learning style—and a unique schedule. That’s why Walden offers you more than one way to learn.\n\nCOURSE BASED\nInstructor-led\nIdeal if you prefer predictability, deadlines and traditional learning format.\nStarts on May 26, 2025\n\n$46,980\nComplete in 48 months*\n\nPay by the course\n\nPre-set schedule\n\nInstructor-led courses\n\nTempo Learning®\nSelf-paced\nIdeal if you’re a self-motivated learner with strong time management skills.\nStarts on May 05, 2025\n\n$15,000\nComplete in 16 months*\n\n3-month subscription pricing\n\nFlexible schedule\n\nPersonal Academic Coach.  PROGRAM OUTCOMES', 'url': 'https://www.waldenu.edu/online-bachelors-programs/bs-in-business-administration', 'url_path': '/online-bachelors-programs/'}]' >>>>>>>>>>>>>>
