sor and SCORE mentor\n   - Specializes in business management and disaster preparedness\n\nThese faculty members bring valuable insights and support to the BS in Business Administration program at Walden University.\n\nIf you have any more questions about the faculty or any other aspect of the program, feel free to ask!', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}), HumanMessage(content='what is there education', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}), AIMessage(content="### Faculty Education for BS in Business Administration Program at Walden University\n\n1. **Dr. Gary Griffith:**\n   - Doctor of Business Administration (DBA)\n   - Specializes in information systems management and technology\n\n2. **Dr. Shannon Lynch:**\n   - Bachelor's in Business Administration (BSBA)\n   - Certified HR Professional through SHRM\n   - Expertise in Human Resources and education\n\n3. **Dr. Harry Kemp:**\n   - Specific education details not provided\n\nIf you need more information about the faculty's education or any other program-related queries, feel free to ask!", additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}), HumanMessage(content='what is the eligibility criteria cyber security?', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}), AIMessage(content="### Eligibility Criteria for MS in Cybersecurity Program at Walden University\n\n- **Bachelor's Degree**: Typically, a bachelor's degree or higher is required for admission to the MS in Cybersecurity program.\n  \n- **Specific Requirements**:\n  1. **Educational Background**: A background in IT, computer science, or a related field may be beneficial.\n  2. **Work Experience**: Some programs may require relevant work experience in the field of cybersecurity.\n  3. **Additional Criteria**: Other specific criteria may vary, so it's best to contact an Enrollment Specialist at 844-529-2438 for personalized information.\n\n- **Admission Process**: Walden University offers a streamlined admissions process with no application fee and easy credit transfer options.\n\nIf you have more questions about the eligibility criteria for the MS in Cybersecurity program or need further details, feel free to ask!", additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}), HumanMessage(content='I did B.Tech from IIT Mumbai, do you think I am eligible?', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}), AIMessage(content='### Eligibility for MS in Cybersecurity Program at Walden University\n\n- Having a B.Tech degree from IIT Mumbai would likely meet the educational background requirement for the program.\n- For personalized information on eligibility criteria and a detailed assessment, contact an Enrollment Specialist at 844-529-2438.\n\nIf you have any more questions or need further assistance, feel free to ask!', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}), HumanMessage(content='do I get any scholarship for this course?', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}), AIMessage(content='### Scholarships for MS in Cybersecurity Program at Walden University\n\n1. **Believe & Achieve Scholarship**\n   - Available to help reduce tuition costs for the MS in Cybersecurity program.\n   \n2. **Other Scholarship Opportunities**\n   - Explore additional scholarships and grants offered by Walden University.\n   \n3. **Contact for More Information**\n   - For specific details on scholarships and financial aid options, contact an Enrollment Specialist at 844-529-2438.\n\nIf you have any more questions or need further assistance, feel free to ask!', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}), HumanMessage(content='what is the accommodation support I can get as I am coming from India to join this course?', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}), AIMessage(content='### Accommodation Support for International Students at Walden University\n\n- **Physical Accommodations:** \n  - As an online university, Walden University does not provide physical accommodations for students coming from India or any other country.\n\n- **Support Services for International Students:**\n  - **Academic Advising:** Guidance on course selection and academic success.\n  - **Career Services:** Assistance with career planning and job search strategies.\n  - **Technical Support:** Help with navigating online platforms and tools.\n  - **Access to Online Resources:** Library resources, research support, and more.\n\n- **International Student Support Team:**\n  - For specific questions or assistance with transitioning to online learning from India, reach out to the International Student Support team at Walden University.\n\nFeel free to reach out if you have any more questions or need further assistance!', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}), HumanMessage(content='which data visualization technology i would learn by this course?', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}), AIMessage(content='### Data Visualization Technology in the MS in Data Science Program at Walden University\n\n- Students in the MS in Data Science program at Walden University will learn data visualization technologies such as:\n  1. Tableau\n  2. Power BI\n  3. Other industry-standard tools\n\nThese technologies are essential for effectively presenting and communicating insights derived from data analysis in a visually engaging and informative manner.\n\nIf you have any more questions or need further details, feel free to ask!', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}), HumanMessage(content='which data visualization technology i would learn by cyber security course?', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}), AIMessage(content='### Data Visualization Technology in the MS in Cybersecurity Program at Walden University\n\n- The MS in Cybersecurity program at Walden University focuses on cybersecurity technology, threat simulations, and practical skills related to cybersecurity.\n- While specific data visualization technologies are not explicitly mentioned, the program may cover visualization tools or techniques relevant to cybersecurity analysis and reporting.\n- For more detailed information on the specific data visualization technologies covered in the program, it is recommended to reach out to the program faculty or advisors for further clarification.\n\nIf you have any more questions or need further assistance, feel free to ask!', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}), HumanMessage(content='who are the famous faculties are associated with this course?', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}), AIMessage(content="### Famous Faculty Associated with the MS in Cybersecurity Program at Walden University\n\n1. **Dr. Robert Duhainy**:\n   - Core Faculty in the College of Management and Human Potential\n   - Doctor of Information Technology (DIT)\n   - Extensive experience in designing and implementing wireless and cellular networks, technology, and computer security\n   - Specializes in cybersecurity, blockchain technologies, secure coding, and more\n\n2. **Dr. Gary Griffith**:\n   - Academic Coordinator in the College of Management and Human Potential\n   - Doctor of Business Administration (DBA)\n   - Expertise in information systems management and technology\n   - Played a key role in Walden University's designation as an NSA Center in Academic Excellence in Cyber Defense\n\nThese faculty members bring a wealth of experience and knowledge to the MS in Cybersecurity program at Walden University. If you have any more questions or need further information, feel free to ask!", additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={})]' for
