2025-04-26 00:20:15,561 - walden_rag - INFO - Data from vectore DB: '[{'_additional': {'certainty': 0.749704897403717, 'distance': 0.5005902}, 'doc_id': '1-1-chunk-1', 'source': 'walden_university', 'text': "More information for international applicants. Questions about the courses you will take? We believe you can achieve your goals and we are here to support you along your journey. Request information to learn more about scholarships and financial aid for those who apply and qualify. Walden offers tuition savings options that can make your goals more attainable. Discover savings opportunities by exploring our scholarships and grants, for those who apply and qualify. Time to completion varies by student, depending on individual progress and credits transferred, if applicable. Tuition and time to complete may be reduced if transfer credits are accepted, or if you receive grants, scholarships, or other tuition reductions. Walden may accept up to 20 transfer credits. For a personalized estimate of the number of your transfer credits that Walden would accept, call an Enrollment Specialist at844-529-2438. Books and materials are not included and may cost up to an additional $1,000 and $1,400. PROGRAM OUTCOMES Our online master's in data science program integrates core business, compliance, and management principles with the rigorous, hands-on training you need to excel in your field. Explore machine learning as you discover how to collect, analyze, and visualize an ever-growing volume of data from information systems. Learn to share insights with stakeholders to empower better decision-making. Work toward becoming the voice of data responsibility and the go-to data expert in your organization and beyond. Career Outlook Now more than ever, businesses need data scientists to help them interpret and leverage a growing volume of raw data. An online data science degree program can help provide you with the hands-on training and specialized technical knowledge necessary to fill this pressing need.", 'url': 'https://www.waldenu.edu/online-masters-programs/ms-in-data-science', 'url_path': '/online-masters-programs/ms-in-data-science'}, {'_additional': {'certainty': 0.7372473478317261, 'distance': 0.5255053}, 'doc_id': '5-0-chunk-1', 'source': '', 'text': 'Online Bachelor’s Programs\nDiscover online bachelor’s degree programs that can help advance your career .Turn Your Ambition Into Achievement With Walden Wayfinder™\nYour journey of change doesn’t have to be a solo mission. Follow Walden Wayfinder™, a guided, all-inclusive path that begins with your destination in mind. You won’t just earn your online bachelor’s degree; you’ll get a personalized, step-by-step road map to a thriving career. From exclusive tuition savings to integrated career planning from Day 1, Walden takes the guesswork out of preparing for your future. You bring your dreams and ambitions—we’ll show you the way forward. Program Variety\n\n.Transfer of Credit\n\nTransfer up to 75% of credits required for your degree program from past college courses, military service, or an associate degree.Walden Undergraduate Academy®\n\nThis dedicated online learning track offers support, tuition savings, and resources for those without previous college credit.Career Resources\n\nTake advantage of our Career Planning and Development Center for one-on-one guidance, networking events, essential job search tools, and more.Applying is Easy', 'url': 'https://www.waldenu.edu/online-bachelors-programs', 'url_path': '/online-bachelors-programs/'}, {'_additional': {'certainty': 0.7305571436882019, 'distance': 0.5388857}, 'doc_id': '1-0-chunk-2', 'source': 'walden_university', 'text': " consumers through responsible data management practices. STRENGTHEN YOUR RESUME Gain advanced data skills that industry trends show employers want and need in their IT workforce. Earning your MS in Data Science degree online is a bold step forward on your professional path. Walden makes it easier with our streamlined admissions process that includes: No application fee Easy credit transfer Program Admission Considerations: A bachelor's degree or higher. General Admission Requirements: Completed online application and transcripts. We believe you can achieve your goals and we are here to support you along your journey.", 'url': 'https://www.waldenu.edu/online-masters-programs/ms-in-data-science', 'url_path': '/online-masters-programs/ms-in-data-science'}, {'_additional': {'certainty': 0.7180673480033875, 'distance': 0.5638653}, 'doc_id': '6-2-chunk-7', 'source': '', 'text': '350 per quarter hour\t\n$63,350\n\nProgram Fee\tPer quarter\t$180\t\n$2,880\n\n$66,230**\nBELIEVE & ACHIEVE SCHOLARSHIP\n\nYOUR TUITION\t-$19,250\n\n$46,980*. Choose Your Concentration\nChoose from three BS in Communication specializations to focus on the career and future you want. Healing, Hierarchy, Healthcare, and Wholeness. Organizational Society, Branding, and Global Citizenship. Possibilities, Problems, and the Human Condition. PROGRAM OUTCOMES\n\nMaster the Science of Strategic Communication\nIn our online bachelor’s degree program, you’ll explore the role and power of communication throughout all facets of human interaction. Coursework covers topics such as interpersonal communication, group communication, digital storytelling, and intercultural communication. Learn what it takes to create a personal identity, sell ideas to others, speak persuasively in public, and analyze messages from mass media. Build a highly transferable skill set that benefits you both in your personal life and in your career endeavors.\n\nCareer Outlook\nCommunication plays a central role in creating and sustaining interpersonal relationships, organizations, cultures, and global societies. In the age of digitization and automation, communicating clearly and making meaningful human connections has become even more important.', 'url': 'https://www.waldenu.edu/online-bachelors-programs/bs-in-communication', 'url_path': '/online-bachelors-programs/'}, {'_additional': {'certainty': 0.7151438295841217, 'distance': 0.56971234}, 'doc_id': '6-2-chunk-6', 'source': '', 'text': '4001 - Intercultural Communication* (5 credits)\nStudents may take this as a non-degree course.\nConcentration Courses (0–25 credits)\nThese courses are dependent upon the particular concentration. Please see the course list on each concentration page.\n\nGeneral Program\n Concentration in Healing, Hierarchy, Healthcare, and Wholeness\n Concentration in Organizational Society, Branding, and Global Citizenship\n Concentration in Possibilities, Problems, and the Human Condition\nElectives (55–80 credits)\nElectives are dependent upon the particular concentration. Please see the elective requirements on each concentration page.\n\nCapstone Course (5 credits)\nCOMM 4901 - Communication Capstone (5 credits). Streamlined Admissions Process\nEarning your BS in Communication degree online is a bold step forward on your professional path. Walden makes it easier with our streamlined admissions process that includes:\n\nNo application fee\n\nEasy credit transfer\n\nNo essay. Admission Criteria. Admission is considered for adult students who hold a high school diploma or its equivalent. Applicants must also meet one of the following criteria:\n\nYou are 21 years of age or older.\nYou are less than 21 years of age with at least 12 quarter credits.\nYou are an active member of the military or a veteran with documentation of service. the fees structure Curriculum Component\tRequirements\tCost\tAmount\nTuition\t181 quarter credit hours\t$350 per quarter hour\t\n$63,350\n\nProgram Fee\tPer quarter\t$180\t\n$2,880\n\n$66,230**\nBELIEVE & ACHIEVE SCHOLARSHIP\n\nYOUR TUITION\t-$19,250', 'url': 'https://www.waldenu.edu/online-bachelors-programs/bs-in-communication', 'url_path': '/online-bachelors-programs/'}, {'_additional': {'certainty': 0.7101656496524811, 'distance': 0.5796687}, 'doc_id': '6-1-chunk-6', 'source': '', 'text': ' She was also a school administrator for a number of years and has the unique background of both an educator and a human resource practitioner.\n\nCourses Taught\nHRMG 4201 - Strategic Human Resource Management\n\nHRMG 3001 - Human Resource Management\n\nHRMG 4203 - HRM: Analysis & Problems\n\nHRMG 4202 - Human Resource Development & Change\n\nEducation\nBS, University of Central Floridsa\n\nMA, Webster University\n\nMS, Walden University\n\nEdS, NovaSotheastern University\n\nEdD, University of Sarasota/Argosy\n\nPublic Service\nAustin City Limits , Volunteer - Austin\n\nAwards / Honors\nOutstanding Principal Award, Eanes ISD, 2001\n\nPublications\nLynch, S. (2011). Answering the Critics of Online Education. www.NAS.org', 'url': 'https://academics.waldenu.edu/catalog/management-human-potential/undergraduate/bachelor-science-business-administration', 'url_path': '/online-bachelors-programs/'}, {'_additional': {'certainty': 0.7090439796447754, 'distance': 0.58191204}, 'doc_id': '1-0-chunk-1', 'source': 'walden_university', 'text': "You offer total 5 programs = 3 MS and 2 BS program there is the list of all programs, MS programs =  Data Science, Cybersecurity, Criminal Justice. BS programs = Bachelor’s in Business Administration, BS in Communication. Title: MS in Data Science | Walden University Description: Walden online MS in Data Science prepares you to make informed decisions and solve complex problems. MS in Data Science. Do you want to help organizations use big data to understand the present and improve the future? Prepare to pursue an engaging career in data science with Walden MS in Data Science program. Taught by subject matter experts, our curriculum equips you with hands-on experience using industry-leading tools in today's latest cloud environments. You'll study practical, sought-after skills to help you become even more effective in your job. Our online master's in data science program also prepares you to use big data in an ethical way so you can drive meaningful change for your employer and society at large. An online data science degree prepares students to use digital data and tools to solve critical, real-world problems in business and industry. BECOME MORE VALUABLE AT WORK Work with industry-standard tools in the most common cloud environments, such as IBM and Amazon Web Services (AWS). MASTER LEADING-EDGE TOOLS Work with industry-standard tools in the most common cloud environments, such as IBM and Amazon Web Services (AWS). LEARN TO USE DATA RESPONSIBLY Explore how to protect your organization and consumers through responsible data management practices. STRENGTHEN YOUR RESUME Gain advanced data skills that industry trends show employers want and need in their IT workforce. Earning your MS in Data Science degree online is a bold step forward on your professional path.", 'url': 'https://www.waldenu.edu/online-masters-programs/ms-in-data-science', 'url_path': '/online-masters-programs/ms-in-data-science'}, {'_additional': {'certainty': 0.7042243778705597, 'distance': 0.59155124}, 'doc_id': '3-1-chunk-1', 'source': 'walden_university', 'text': "Streamlined Admissions Process\nEarning your MS in Cybersecurity degree online is a big decision, which is why we’ve streamlined and simplified the admissions process. Start your journey with:\n\nNo application fee\n\nEasy credit transfer\n\nNo essay. Admission Criteria : Program Admission Considerations: A bachelor's degree or higher. Tuition Breakdown \nWalden offers tuition savings options that can make your goals more attainable. Discover savings opportunities by exploring our scholarships and grants, for those who apply and qualify.\n\nBelieve & Achieve Scholarship®\n\nWalden grants\n\nFederal and state grants   Curriculum Component\tRequirements\tCost\tAmount\nTuition\t45 quarter credit hours\t$565 per quarter hour\t\n$25,425\n\nProgram Fee\tPer quarter\t$180\t\n$900\n\n$26,325**\nBELIEVE & ACHIEVE SCHOLARSHIP\n\nYOUR TUITION\t\n-$5,650\n\n$20,675*\n\n. Books and materials are not included and may cost up to an additional $1,000 and $1,400.   **Tuition reflects the minimum time to completion. Time to completion varies by student, depending on individual progress and credits transferred, if applicable. Tuition and time to complete may be reduced if transfer credits are accepted, or if you receive grants, scholarships, or other tuition reductions. Walden may accept up to 20 transfer credits. For a personalized estimate of the number of your transfer credits that Walden would accept. PROGRAM OUTCOMES", 'url': 'https://www.waldenu.edu/online-masters-programs/ms-in-cybersecurity', 'url_path': '/online-masters-programs/'}, {'_additional': {'certainty': 0.7018272876739502, 'distance': 0.5963454}, 'doc_id': '6-0-chunk-3', 'source': '', 'text': ' the admissions process. Start your journey with:\n\nNo application fee\n\nEasy credit transfer\n\nNo essay.  Admission Criteria = Admission is considered for adult students who hold a high school diploma or its equivalent. Applicants must also meet one of the following criteria:\n\nYou are 21 years of age or older.\nYou are less than 21 years of age with at least 12 quarter credits.\nYou are an active member of the military or a veteran with documentation of service. Choose Your Concentration\nChoose from eight BS in Business Administration concentrations to focus on the career and future you want. Accounting,Finance,General Program,Healthcare Management,Human Resource Management,Management,Marketing,Small Business Management.  tuition and fees : Tuition Breakdown\nWe know cost is a major consideration when exploring online BS in Business Administration programs. That’s why Walden offers opportunities to reduce your tuition through:\n\nExperience-based credits\n\nSpecial tuition savings\n\nBelieve & Achieve Scholarship. General Program Concentration Course-Based Learning = Curriculum Component\tRequirements\tCost\tAmount\nTuition\t181 quarter credit hours\t$350 per quarter hour\t\n$63,350\n\nProgram Fee\tPer quarter\t$180\t\n$2,880\n\n$66,230**\n\nBELIEVE & ACHIEVE SCHOLARSHIP\n\nYOUR TUITION\t\n-$19,250\n\n$46,980*\n\n. Books and materials are not included and may cost up to an additional $5,500. Tempo Learning = Progress at Your Pace. Control Your Cost.\n\nWalden’s Tempo Learning® programs follow a subscription-based pricing format. Students are billed a flat-rate for each 3-month subscription term. All pricing is represented in U.S. dollars and is subject to change.', 'url': 'https://www.waldenu.edu/online-bachelors-programs/bs-in-business-administration', 'url_path': '/online-bachelors-programs/'}, {'_additional': {'certainty': 0.6887229681015015, 'distance': 0.62255406}, 'doc_id': '6-2-chunk-8', 'source': '', 'text': ' in your career endeavors.\n\nCareer Outlook\nCommunication plays a central role in creating and sustaining interpersonal relationships, organizations, cultures, and global societies. In the age of digitization and automation, communicating clearly and making meaningful human connections has become even more important.\n\nAn online bachelor’s in communication degree equips you with a practical, versatile skill set that’s in demand and applicable across all industries. According to the National Association of Colleges and Employers’ (NACE) Job Outlook 2021, employers rank written and verbal communication skills among the most important attributes they look for in a job candidate.1 And employment in media and communication occupations is projected to grow 14% through 2030, according to the Bureau of Labor Statistics.2\n\nCareer options may require additional experience, training, licensure, or other factors beyond the successful completion of this online communication degree program. Learning Outcomes\nAs a graduate of Walden’s BS in Communication program, you’ll be prepared to:\n\nArticulate the importance of thoughtful message creation and delivery in personal, family, work, social, political and community life.\n\nDemonstrate active listening skills to effectively receive, process, and respond to verbal and nonverbal communication delivered through various communication channels.\n\nDemonstrate active listening skills to effectively receive, process, and respond to verbal and nonverbal communication delivered through various communication channels.\n\nIdentify the influences that organizational and societal structures, practices, and paradigms have on access to communication modalities, as well as the content of messages delivered in social media, political discourse, mass communication and interpersonal interactions.', 'url': 'https://www.waldenu.edu/online-bachelors-programs/bs-in-communication', 'url_path': '/online-bachelors-programs/'}]' >>>>>>>>>>>>>>
