g our scholarships and grants, for those who apply and qualify. Time to completion varies by student, depending on individual progress and credits transferred, if applicable. Tuition and time to complete may be reduced if transfer credits are accepted, or if you receive grants, scholarships, or other tuition reductions. Walden may accept up to 20 transfer credits. For a personalized estimate of the number of your transfer credits that Walden would accept, call an Enrollment Specialist at844-529-2438. Books and materials are not included and may cost up to an additional $1,000 and $1,400. PROGRAM OUTCOMES Our online master's in data science program integrates core business, compliance, and management principles with the rigorous, hands-on training you need to excel in your field. Explore machine learning as you discover how to collect, analyze, and visualize an ever-growing volume of data from information systems. Learn to share insights with stakeholders to empower better decision-making. Work toward becoming the voice of data responsibility and the go-to data expert in your organization and beyond. Career Outlook Now more than ever, businesses need data scientists to help them interpret and leverage a growing volume of raw data. An online data science degree program can help provide you with the hands-on training and specialized technical knowledge necessary to fill this pressing need.", 'url': 'https://www.waldenu.edu/online-masters-programs/ms-in-data-science', 'url_path': '/online-masters-programs/ms-in-data-science'}, {'_additional': {'certainty': 0.8271917998790741, 'distance': 0.3456164}, 'doc_id': '6-2-chunk-1', 'source': '', 'text': 'Online BS in Communication\nMaster practical, applicable communication skills you can use in any setting—from professional endeavors to everyday interactions. why walden Learn to Better Connect, Engage, and Motivate With a BS in Communication\nNo matter where life takes you, your success often depends on being able to communicate effectively. Walden’s BS in Communication program focuses on the practical tools you need to make your voice heard and your message understood. First, build a strong communication foundation that can enhance your personal and professional growth. Then, apply these principles to a program concentration that reflects your specific area of interest.\n\nAn online communication degree prepares students to write, share, and present ideas and messaging impactfully to their audience. BUILD ACTIONABLE SKILLS\n\nApply theory to learn practical skills and concepts you can begin using immediately—at work and in your daily life. WALDEN UNDERGRADUATE ACADEMY®\n\nGet dedicated support, tuition savings,1 and resources if you have no prior college credits. Learn with other first-time college students.\n\nPERSONALIZE YOUR LEARNING\n\nChoose our General Program or one of three concentrations to build skills in an area you’re passionate about. Program Details\n\nTake a Closer Look\nLearn more about Walden’s BS in Communication program, from our streamlined admissions requirements to our rigorous curriculum. Curriculum – General Program\nDegree Completion Requirements', 'url': 'https://www.waldenu.edu/online-bachelors-programs/bs-in-communication', 'url_path': '/online-bachelors-programs/'}, {'_additional': {'certainty': 0.8188617527484894, 'distance': 0.3622765}, 'doc_id': '1-0-chunk-1', 'source': 'walden_university', 'text': "You offer total 5 programs = 3 MS and 2 BS program there is the list of all programs, MS programs =  Data Science, Cybersecurity, Criminal Justice. BS programs = Bachelor’s in Business Administration, BS in Communication. Title: MS in Data Science | Walden University Description: Walden online MS in Data Science prepares you to make informed decisions and solve complex problems. MS in Data Science. Do you want to help organizations use big data to understand the present and improve the future? Prepare to pursue an engaging career in data science with Walden MS in Data Science program. Taught by subject matter experts, our curriculum equips you with hands-on experience using industry-leading tools in today's latest cloud environments. You'll study practical, sought-after skills to help you become even more effective in your job. Our online master's in data science program also prepares you to use big data in an ethical way so you can drive meaningful change for your employer and society at large. An online data science degree prepares students to use digital data and tools to solve critical, real-world problems in business and industry. BECOME MORE VALUABLE AT WORK Work with industry-standard tools in the most common cloud environments, such as IBM and Amazon Web Services (AWS). MASTER LEADING-EDGE TOOLS Work with industry-standard tools in the most common cloud environments, such as IBM and Amazon Web Services (AWS). LEARN TO USE DATA RESPONSIBLY Explore how to protect your organization and consumers through responsible data management practices. STRENGTHEN YOUR RESUME Gain advanced data skills that industry trends show employers want and need in their IT workforce. Earning your MS in Data Science degree online is a bold step forward on your professional path.", 'url': 'https://www.waldenu.edu/online-masters-programs/ms-in-data-science', 'url_path': '/online-masters-programs/ms-in-data-science'}, {'_additional': {'certainty': 0.8123392164707184, 'distance': 0.37532157}, 'doc_id': '1-0-chunk-2', 'source': 'walden_university', 'text': " consumers through responsible data management practices. STRENGTHEN YOUR RESUME Gain advanced data skills that industry trends show employers want and need in their IT workforce. Earning your MS in Data Science degree online is a bold step forward on your professional path. Walden makes it easier with our streamlined admissions process that includes: No application fee Easy credit transfer Program Admission Considerations: A bachelor's degree or higher. General Admission Requirements: Completed online application and transcripts. We believe you can achieve your goals and we are here to support you along your journey.", 'url': 'https://www.waldenu.edu/online-masters-programs/ms-in-data-science', 'url_path': '/online-masters-programs/ms-in-data-science'}, {'_additional': {'certainty': 0.8119124174118042, 'distance': 0.37617517}, 'doc_id': '5-0-chunk-2', 'source': '', 'text': ' learning track offers support, tuition savings, and resources for those without previous college credit.Career Resources\n\nTake advantage of our Career Planning and Development Center for one-on-one guidance, networking events, essential job search tools, and more.Applying is Easy\n\nNo application fee, essay, or SAT or ACT score is required for admission. Bachelor’s Programs BS in Business Administration, BS in Communication.  An Accredited University\nQuality matters—especially when it comes to your education. Walden is accredited by The Higher Learning Commission and committed to maintaining the highest standards of excellence. Flexibility to Fit Your Schedule\nAt Walden, we are dedicated to offering education options designed to fit the needs of working professionals like you. That is why we offer a wide range of learning options, including a standard, course-based experience, and Tempo Learning®. COURSE BASED\nInstructor-led\nEngage in a course-by-course experience, where you progress on a predetermined schedule. This format allows you to learn alongside your peers, participating in weekly discussions and meeting established deadlines for assignments. Your cost is based on how many credits you need to complete your program.\n\nIdeal for students who are newer to online education and prefer structure, working with others, and having set deadlines.\n\nStarts on May 26\n\nRegister and pay by course.\n\nCourse lengths are predetermined, based on program.\n\nFaculty guide you through each course.\n\nScheduled due dates allow you make steady progress.', 'url': 'https://www.waldenu.edu/online-bachelors-programs', 'url_path': '/online-bachelors-programs/'}, {'_additional': {'certainty': 0.7960034012794495, 'distance': 0.4079932}, 'doc_id': '6-0-chunk-3', 'source': '', 'text': ' the admissions process. Start your journey with:\n\nNo application fee\n\nEasy credit transfer\n\nNo essay.  Admission Criteria = Admission is considered for adult students who hold a high school diploma or its equivalent. Applicants must also meet one of the following criteria:\n\nYou are 21 years of age or older.\nYou are less than 21 years of age with at least 12 quarter credits.\nYou are an active member of the military or a veteran with documentation of service. Choose Your Concentration\nChoose from eight BS in Business Administration concentrations to focus on the career and future you want. Accounting,Finance,General Program,Healthcare Management,Human Resource Management,Management,Marketing,Small Business Management.  tuition and fees : Tuition Breakdown\nWe know cost is a major consideration when exploring online BS in Business Administration programs. That’s why Walden offers opportunities to reduce your tuition through:\n\nExperience-based credits\n\nSpecial tuition savings\n\nBelieve & Achieve Scholarship. General Program Concentration Course-Based Learning = Curriculum Component\tRequirements\tCost\tAmount\nTuition\t181 quarter credit hours\t$350 per quarter hour\t\n$63,350\n\nProgram Fee\tPer quarter\t$180\t\n$2,880\n\n$66,230**\n\nBELIEVE & ACHIEVE SCHOLARSHIP\n\nYOUR TUITION\t\n-$19,250\n\n$46,980*\n\n. Books and materials are not included and may cost up to an additional $5,500. Tempo Learning = Progress at Your Pace. Control Your Cost.\n\nWalden’s Tempo Learning® programs follow a subscription-based pricing format. Students are billed a flat-rate for each 3-month subscription term. All pricing is represented in U.S. dollars and is subject to change.', 'url': 'https://www.waldenu.edu/online-bachelors-programs/bs-in-business-administration', 'url_path': '/online-bachelors-programs/'}, {'_additional': {'certainty': 0.7959079742431641, 'distance': 0.40818405}, 'doc_id': '3-1-chunk-1', 'source': 'walden_university', 'text': "Streamlined Admissions Process\nEarning your MS in Cybersecurity degree online is a big decision, which is why we’ve streamlined and simplified the admissions process. Start your journey with:\n\nNo application fee\n\nEasy credit transfer\n\nNo essay. Admission Criteria : Program Admission Considerations: A bachelor's degree or higher. Tuition Breakdown \nWalden offers tuition savings options that can make your goals more attainable. Discover savings opportunities by exploring our scholarships and grants, for those who apply and qualify.\n\nBelieve & Achieve Scholarship®\n\nWalden grants\n\nFederal and state grants   Curriculum Component\tRequirements\tCost\tAmount\nTuition\t45 quarter credit hours\t$565 per quarter hour\t\n$25,425\n\nProgram Fee\tPer quarter\t$180\t\n$900\n\n$26,325**\nBELIEVE & ACHIEVE SCHOLARSHIP\n\nYOUR TUITION\t\n-$5,650\n\n$20,675*\n\n. Books and materials are not included and may cost up to an additional $1,000 and $1,400.   **Tuition reflects the minimum time to completion. Time to completion varies by student, depending on individual progress and credits transferred, if applicable. Tuition and time to complete may be reduced if transfer credits are accepted, or if you receive grants, scholarships, or other tuition reductions. Walden may accept up to 20 transfer credits. For a personalized estimate of the number of your transfer credits that Walden would accept. PROGRAM OUTCOMES", 'url': 'https://www.waldenu.edu/online-masters-programs/ms-in-cybersecurity', 'url_path': '/online-masters-programs/'}, {'_additional': {'certainty': 0.7875738739967346, 'distance': 0.42485225}, 'doc_id': '6-2-chunk-8', 'source': '', 'text': ' in your career endeavors.\n\nCareer Outlook\nCommunication plays a central role in creating and sustaining interpersonal relationships, organizations, cultures, and global societies. In the age of digitization and automation, communicating clearly and making meaningful human connections has become even more important.\n\nAn online bachelor’s in communication degree equips you with a practical, versatile skill set that’s in demand and applicable across all industries. According to the National Association of Colleges and Employers’ (NACE) Job Outlook 2021, employers rank written and verbal communication skills among the most important attributes they look for in a job candidate.1 And employment in media and communication occupations is projected to grow 14% through 2030, according to the Bureau of Labor Statistics.2\n\nCareer options may require additional experience, training, licensure, or other factors beyond the successful completion of this online communication degree program. Learning Outcomes\nAs a graduate of Walden’s BS in Communication program, you’ll be prepared to:\n\nArticulate the importance of thoughtful message creation and delivery in personal, family, work, social, political and community life.\n\nDemonstrate active listening skills to effectively receive, process, and respond to verbal and nonverbal communication delivered through various communication channels.\n\nDemonstrate active listening skills to effectively receive, process, and respond to verbal and nonverbal communication delivered through various communication channels.\n\nIdentify the influences that organizational and societal structures, practices, and paradigms have on access to communication modalities, as well as the content of messages delivered in social media, political discourse, mass communication and interpersonal interactions.', 'url': 'https://www.waldenu.edu/online-bachelors-programs/bs-in-communication', 'url_path': '/online-bachelors-programs/'}, {'_additional': {'certainty': 0.7875209450721741, 'distance': 0.4249581}, 'doc_id': '6-2-chunk-6', 'source': '', 'text': '4001 - Intercultural Communication* (5 credits)\nStudents may take this as a non-degree course.\nConcentration Courses (0–25 credits)\nThese courses are dependent upon the particular concentration. Please see the course list on each concentration page.\n\nGeneral Program\n Concentration in Healing, Hierarchy, Healthcare, and Wholeness\n Concentration in Organizational Society, Branding, and Global Citizenship\n Concentration in Possibilities, Problems, and the Human Condition\nElectives (55–80 credits)\nElectives are dependent upon the particular concentration. Please see the elective requirements on each concentration page.\n\nCapstone Course (5 credits)\nCOMM 4901 - Communication Capstone (5 credits). Streamlined Admissions Process\nEarning your BS in Communication degree online is a bold step forward on your professional path. Walden makes it easier with our streamlined admissions process that includes:\n\nNo application fee\n\nEasy credit transfer\n\nNo essay. Admission Criteria. Admission is considered for adult students who hold a high school diploma or its equivalent. Applicants must also meet one of the following criteria:\n\nYou are 21 years of age or older.\nYou are less than 21 years of age with at least 12 quarter credits.\nYou are an active member of the military or a veteran with documentation of service. the fees structure Curriculum Component\tRequirements\tCost\tAmount\nTuition\t181 quarter credit hours\t$350 per quarter hour\t\n$63,350\n\nProgram Fee\tPer quarter\t$180\t\n$2,880\n\n$66,230**\nBELIEVE & ACHIEVE SCHOLARSHIP\n\nYOUR TUITION\t-$19,250', 'url': 'https://www.waldenu.edu/online-bachelors-programs/bs-in-communication', 'url_path': '/online-bachelors-programs/'}]' >>>>>>>>>>>>>>
