p organizations use big data to understand the present and improve the future? Prepare to pursue an engaging career in data science with Walden MS in Data Science program. Taught by subject matter experts, our curriculum equips you with hands-on experience using industry-leading tools in today's latest cloud environments. You'll study practical, sought-after skills to help you become even more effective in your job. Our online master's in data science program also prepares you to use big data in an ethical way so you can drive meaningful change for your employer and society at large. An online data science degree prepares students to use digital data and tools to solve critical, real-world problems in business and industry. BECOME MORE VALUABLE AT WORK Work with industry-standard tools in the most common cloud environments, such as IBM and Amazon Web Services (AWS). MASTER LEADING-EDGE TOOLS Work with industry-standard tools in the most common cloud environments, such as IBM and Amazon Web Services (AWS). LEARN TO USE DATA RESPONSIBLY Explore how to protect your organization and consumers through responsible data management practices. STRENGTHEN YOUR RESUME Gain advanced data skills that industry trends show employers want and need in their IT workforce. Earning your MS in Data Science degree online is a bold step forward on your professional path.", 'url': 'https://www.waldenu.edu/online-masters-programs/ms-in-data-science', 'url_path': '/online-masters-programs/ms-in-data-science'}, {'_additional': {'certainty': 0.7673248946666718, 'distance': 0.4653502}, 'doc_id': '4-2-chunk-1', 'source': 'walden_university', 'text': "Streamlined Admissions Process\nEarning your Online Master’s Degree in Criminal Justice is a big decision, which is why we’ve streamlined and simplified the admissions process. Start your journey with:\n\nNo application fee\n\nEasy credit transfer\n\nNo essay. Admission Criteria Program Admission Considerations: A bachelor's degree or higher.  Fees structure Curriculum Component\tRequirements\tCost\tAmount\nTuition\t48 total quarter credit hours\t$560 per quarter hour\t\n$26,880\n\nProgram Fee\tPer quarter\t$180\t\n$900\n\n$27,780**\n\nBELIEVE & ACHIEVE SCHOLARSHIP\n\nYOUR TUITION\t\n-$5,600\n\n$22,180*\n\n. Tuition and fees are subject to change. Books and materials are not included and may cost between $1,000 and $1,400.  With Tempo Learning, you may be able to complete your MS in Criminal Justice degree in as few as 5 months for as low as $7,000. *Represents Tempo Learning® format, Believe & Achieve Scholarship, and the fastest pace of our top 25% transfer students in this program in the Tempo Learning® format. PROGRAM OUTCOMES\n\nWhat’s the Career Impact of Earning Criminal Justice Master’s Degree?\nGraduates of the MS in Criminal Justice program will be well-prepared to seek leadership roles across an array of areas, including law enforcement, courts, corrections, and probation. Possible job titles include:", 'url': 'https://www.waldenu.edu/online-masters-programs/ms-in-criminal-justice', 'url_path': '/online-masters-programs/'}, {'_additional': {'certainty': 0.7534684538841248, 'distance': 0.4930631}, 'doc_id': '6-2-chunk-4', 'source': '', 'text': '–25 credits, depending on concentration)\nElective courses (55–80 credits, depending on concentration)\nCapstone course (5 credits)\nCurriculum\nGeneral Education Courses (46 credits)\nSee the General Education section of this Walden University Catalog.\n\nNote: A minimum of 60 quarter credits must be completed at the 3000 or 4000 level in order to meet program requirements. In some cases, this means that students will need to select 3000 or 4000 level courses as either general education or elective options. Students should consult their student success advisor if they have questions about individual program requirements.', 'url': 'https://www.waldenu.edu/online-bachelors-programs/bs-in-communication', 'url_path': '/online-bachelors-programs/'}, {'_additional': {'certainty': 0.7518366575241089, 'distance': 0.49632668}, 'doc_id': '5-0-chunk-2', 'source': '', 'text': ' learning track offers support, tuition savings, and resources for those without previous college credit.Career Resources\n\nTake advantage of our Career Planning and Development Center for one-on-one guidance, networking events, essential job search tools, and more.Applying is Easy\n\nNo application fee, essay, or SAT or ACT score is required for admission. Bachelor’s Programs BS in Business Administration, BS in Communication.  An Accredited University\nQuality matters—especially when it comes to your education. Walden is accredited by The Higher Learning Commission and committed to maintaining the highest standards of excellence. Flexibility to Fit Your Schedule\nAt Walden, we are dedicated to offering education options designed to fit the needs of working professionals like you. That is why we offer a wide range of learning options, including a standard, course-based experience, and Tempo Learning®. COURSE BASED\nInstructor-led\nEngage in a course-by-course experience, where you progress on a predetermined schedule. This format allows you to learn alongside your peers, participating in weekly discussions and meeting established deadlines for assignments. Your cost is based on how many credits you need to complete your program.\n\nIdeal for students who are newer to online education and prefer structure, working with others, and having set deadlines.\n\nStarts on May 26\n\nRegister and pay by course.\n\nCourse lengths are predetermined, based on program.\n\nFaculty guide you through each course.\n\nScheduled due dates allow you make steady progress.', 'url': 'https://www.waldenu.edu/online-bachelors-programs', 'url_path': '/online-bachelors-programs/'}]' >>>>>>>>>>>>>>
