ill this pressing need.", 'url': 'https://www.waldenu.edu/online-masters-programs/ms-in-data-science', 'url_path': '/online-masters-programs/ms-in-data-science'}, {'_additional': {'certainty': 0.8103770017623901, 'distance': 0.379246}, 'doc_id': '1-0-chunk-2', 'source': 'walden_university', 'text': " consumers through responsible data management practices. STRENGTHEN YOUR RESUME Gain advanced data skills that industry trends show employers want and need in their IT workforce. Earning your MS in Data Science degree online is a bold step forward on your professional path. Walden makes it easier with our streamlined admissions process that includes: No application fee Easy credit transfer Program Admission Considerations: A bachelor's degree or higher. General Admission Requirements: Completed online application and transcripts. We believe you can achieve your goals and we are here to support you along your journey.", 'url': 'https://www.waldenu.edu/online-masters-programs/ms-in-data-science', 'url_path': '/online-masters-programs/ms-in-data-science'}, {'_additional': {'certainty': 0.8098994493484497, 'distance': 0.3802011}, 'doc_id': '3-1-chunk-1', 'source': 'walden_university', 'text': "Streamlined Admissions Process\nEarning your MS in Cybersecurity degree online is a big decision, which is why we’ve streamlined and simplified the admissions process. Start your journey with:\n\nNo application fee\n\nEasy credit transfer\n\nNo essay. Admission Criteria : Program Admission Considerations: A bachelor's degree or higher. Tuition Breakdown \nWalden offers tuition savings options that can make your goals more attainable. Discover savings opportunities by exploring our scholarships and grants, for those who apply and qualify.\n\nBelieve & Achieve Scholarship®\n\nWalden grants\n\nFederal and state grants   Curriculum Component\tRequirements\tCost\tAmount\nTuition\t45 quarter credit hours\t$565 per quarter hour\t\n$25,425\n\nProgram Fee\tPer quarter\t$180\t\n$900\n\n$26,325**\nBELIEVE & ACHIEVE SCHOLARSHIP\n\nYOUR TUITION\t\n-$5,650\n\n$20,675*\n\n. Books and materials are not included and may cost up to an additional $1,000 and $1,400.   **Tuition reflects the minimum time to completion. Time to completion varies by student, depending on individual progress and credits transferred, if applicable. Tuition and time to complete may be reduced if transfer credits are accepted, or if you receive grants, scholarships, or other tuition reductions. Walden may accept up to 20 transfer credits. For a personalized estimate of the number of your transfer credits that Walden would accept. PROGRAM OUTCOMES", 'url': 'https://www.waldenu.edu/online-masters-programs/ms-in-cybersecurity', 'url_path': '/online-masters-programs/'}, {'_additional': {'certainty': 0.7895883023738861, 'distance': 0.4208234}, 'doc_id': '1-0-chunk-1', 'source': 'walden_university', 'text': "You offer total 5 programs = 3 MS and 2 BS program there is the list of all programs, MS programs =  Data Science, Cybersecurity, Criminal Justice. BS programs = Bachelor’s in Business Administration, BS in Communication. Title: MS in Data Science | Walden University Description: Walden online MS in Data Science prepares you to make informed decisions and solve complex problems. MS in Data Science. Do you want to help organizations use big data to understand the present and improve the future? Prepare to pursue an engaging career in data science with Walden MS in Data Science program. Taught by subject matter experts, our curriculum equips you with hands-on experience using industry-leading tools in today's latest cloud environments. You'll study practical, sought-after skills to help you become even more effective in your job. Our online master's in data science program also prepares you to use big data in an ethical way so you can drive meaningful change for your employer and society at large. An online data science degree prepares students to use digital data and tools to solve critical, real-world problems in business and industry. BECOME MORE VALUABLE AT WORK Work with industry-standard tools in the most common cloud environments, such as IBM and Amazon Web Services (AWS). MASTER LEADING-EDGE TOOLS Work with industry-standard tools in the most common cloud environments, such as IBM and Amazon Web Services (AWS). LEARN TO USE DATA RESPONSIBLY Explore how to protect your organization and consumers through responsible data management practices. STRENGTHEN YOUR RESUME Gain advanced data skills that industry trends show employers want and need in their IT workforce. Earning your MS in Data Science degree online is a bold step forward on your professional path.", 'url': 'https://www.waldenu.edu/online-masters-programs/ms-in-data-science', 'url_path': '/online-masters-programs/ms-in-data-science'}, {'_additional': {'certainty': 0.7691053748130798, 'distance': 0.46178925}, 'doc_id': '6-0-chunk-3', 'source': '', 'text': ' the admissions process. Start your journey with:\n\nNo application fee\n\nEasy credit transfer\n\nNo essay.  Admission Criteria = Admission is considered for adult students who hold a high school diploma or its equivalent. Applicants must also meet one of the following criteria:\n\nYou are 21 years of age or older.\nYou are less than 21 years of age with at least 12 quarter credits.\nYou are an active member of the military or a veteran with documentation of service. Choose Your Concentration\nChoose from eight BS in Business Administration concentrations to focus on the career and future you want. Accounting,Finance,General Program,Healthcare Management,Human Resource Management,Management,Marketing,Small Business Management.  tuition and fees : Tuition Breakdown\nWe know cost is a major consideration when exploring online BS in Business Administration programs. That’s why Walden offers opportunities to reduce your tuition through:\n\nExperience-based credits\n\nSpecial tuition savings\n\nBelieve & Achieve Scholarship. General Program Concentration Course-Based Learning = Curriculum Component\tRequirements\tCost\tAmount\nTuition\t181 quarter credit hours\t$350 per quarter hour\t\n$63,350\n\nProgram Fee\tPer quarter\t$180\t\n$2,880\n\n$66,230**\n\nBELIEVE & ACHIEVE SCHOLARSHIP\n\nYOUR TUITION\t\n-$19,250\n\n$46,980*\n\n. Books and materials are not included and may cost up to an additional $5,500. Tempo Learning = Progress at Your Pace. Control Your Cost.\n\nWalden’s Tempo Learning® programs follow a subscription-based pricing format. Students are billed a flat-rate for each 3-month subscription term. All pricing is represented in U.S. dollars and is subject to change.', 'url': 'https://www.waldenu.edu/online-bachelors-programs/bs-in-business-administration', 'url_path': '/online-bachelors-programs/'}, {'_additional': {'certainty': 0.7629011571407318, 'distance': 0.4741977}, 'doc_id': '1-3-chunk-1', 'source': 'walden_university', 'text': "is beneficial for students to have at least a foundational understanding before pursuing a master's degree in the field. That's because programming helps data scientists to process, analyze, and generate predictions from data. Python, R, and SQL are just a few of the programming languages used to tackle specific tasks. Sifting through and analyzing large datasets is a key part of the job, so the ability to understand one or more of these languages is essential. The fees structure of MS in Data Science program  (Type: financial): Financial/Tuition Information: Tuition - 45 quarter credit hours - $565 per quarter hour - $25,425 Program Fee - Per quarter - $180 - $900 - - - $26,325** Total Cost: $26,325**", 'url': 'https://www.waldenu.edu/online-masters-programs/ms-in-data-science', 'url_path': '/online-masters-programs/ms-in-data-science'}, {'_additional': {'certainty': 0.7449877858161926, 'distance': 0.5100244}, 'doc_id': '5-0-chunk-1', 'source': '', 'text': 'Online Bachelor’s Programs\nDiscover online bachelor’s degree programs that can help advance your career .Turn Your Ambition Into Achievement With Walden Wayfinder™\nYour journey of change doesn’t have to be a solo mission. Follow Walden Wayfinder™, a guided, all-inclusive path that begins with your destination in mind. You won’t just earn your online bachelor’s degree; you’ll get a personalized, step-by-step road map to a thriving career. From exclusive tuition savings to integrated career planning from Day 1, Walden takes the guesswork out of preparing for your future. You bring your dreams and ambitions—we’ll show you the way forward. Program Variety\n\n.Transfer of Credit\n\nTransfer up to 75% of credits required for your degree program from past college courses, military service, or an associate degree.Walden Undergraduate Academy®\n\nThis dedicated online learning track offers support, tuition savings, and resources for those without previous college credit.Career Resources\n\nTake advantage of our Career Planning and Development Center for one-on-one guidance, networking events, essential job search tools, and more.Applying is Easy', 'url': 'https://www.waldenu.edu/online-bachelors-programs', 'url_path': '/online-bachelors-programs/'}, {'_additional': {'certainty': 0.7424235939979553, 'distance': 0.5151528}, 'doc_id': '2-0-chunk-1', 'source': 'walden_university', 'text': "Title: MS in Data Science (Quarter) - Master's Programs - Academics at Walden University Program Website For students beginning their program November 28, 2022 or later. The MS in Data Science program empowers students with the specialized skills needed to turn raw information into valuable business insights. Through courses developed in collaboration with IBM, students focus on: Walden's MS in Data Science program is focused on responsible data management practices and the ethical use of data to address business challenges. Upon completion of the MS in Data Science, students will be able to: List: Evaluate emerging technical developments that apply to data science.. Analyze current technologies that provide practical solutions to data science problems.. Evaluate the role of supporting technologies for data science in data driven decision-making.. Analyze legal, ethical, professional and social issue elements within the domain of data science.. Differentiate how the techniques and tools of big data predictive analytics can be used to add business value in data driven decision-making in the modern work place. List: 45 total quarter credits List: Students may take this as a non-degree course.", 'url': 'https://academics.waldenu.edu/catalog/management-human-potential/masters-programs/master-science/data-science-quarter', 'url_path': '/catalog/management-human-potential/masters-programs/master-science/data-science-quarter'}, {'_additional': {'certainty': 0.7390691041946411, 'distance': 0.5218618}, 'doc_id': '1-2-chunk-1', 'source': 'walden_university', 'text': "in data science online program will be prepared to: Evaluate emerging technical developments that apply to data science. Analyze current technologies that provide practical solutions to data science problems. Explore the role of supporting technologies for data science in data-driven decision-making. Analyze legal, ethical, professional, and social issue elements within the domain of data science. Differentiate how the techniques and tools of big data predictive analytics can be used to add 'business value' in data-driven decision-making in the modern workplace. Below are some of the distinguished faculty members who bring diverse industry expertise and a passion for teaching to the Walden community. faculty name Gail Miles Program Director Dr. Miles taught Computer Science face-to-face for over 25 years starting at the University of Florida. She retired from Lenoir-Rhyne University as Professor Emerita in 2013. She taught IT online since 2000 in a variety of levels and programs. She was the Director of Online Studies for the Masters Programmes of the Department of Computer Science, University of Liverpool in the UK from 2013 to 2019. She is currently the Associate Dean of Masters programs in Information Technology, Doctor of Information Technology, PhD in Management, and Doctor of Business Administration in College of Management and Human Potential for Walden University\nAll of her graduate work was completed at the University of Florida (MEd, EdS, PhD, and MS). The second faculty name Osama Morad Contributing Faculty College of Management and Human Potential Doctor of Information Technology (DIT). Data science is the process of extracting insights from data.", 'url': 'https://www.waldenu.edu/online-masters-programs/ms-in-data-science', 'url_path': '/online-masters-programs/ms-in-data-science'}, {'_additional': {'certainty': 0.7308959364891052, 'distance': 0.5382081}, 'doc_id': '2-0-chunk-2', 'source': 'walden_university', 'text': ".. Differentiate how the techniques and tools of big data predictive analytics can be used to add business value in data driven decision-making in the modern work place. List: 45 total quarter credits List: Students may take this as a non-degree course. Program Curriculum: MS in Data Science (Quarter) - College of Management and Human Potential - Master's Programs - Academics at Walden University Quarter 1 - MDSC 6005 - The Global Technology Environment - 5 credits credits Quarter 2 - MDSC 6401 - Statistical Concepts for Big Data - 5 credits credits MDSC 6245 - Big Data - 5 credits - credits Quarter 3 - MDSC 6265 - Data Mining - 5 credits credits MDSC 6685 - Data Visualization - 5 credits - credits Quarter 4 - MDSC 6665 - Predictive Analytics for Decision Making - 5 credits credits MDSC 6210 - Cloud Computing - 5 credits - credits Quarter 5 -", 'url': 'https://academics.waldenu.edu/catalog/management-human-potential/masters-programs/master-science/data-science-quarter', 'url_path': '/catalog/management-human-potential/masters-programs/master-science/data-science-quarter'}]' >>>>>>>>>>>>>>
