2025-04-26 00:33:12,365 - walden_rag - INFO - Data from vectore DB: '[{'doc_id': '3-2-chunk-3', 'source': 'walden_university', 'text': "uhainy, B. (2021). Ways to Bloom Where You’re Planted. Information Security Professional ISC2\n\nPresentations\nDUHAINY, B. (2022). Cybersecurity Attacks and Countermeasures . FBI Citizens Academy\n\nDuhainy, B. (2022). Infrastructure Security. FBI Citizens Academy Duhainy, B. (2020). Cybersecurity in the age of AI, Automation and GDPR. Walden University. Gary Griffith\nAcademic Coordinator  \nCollege of Management and Human Potential\nDoctor of Business Administration (DBA)   Dr. Gary Griffith started teaching as a contributing faculty for Walden University in the Master of Science in Information Systems Management program in 2011. In 2012 I accepted a core faculty position in the Master of Science in Information Technology program. Since starting my career at Walden University I have taught 16 different courses in BSIT, MISM, MSIT and DIT programs. Most of the courses I teach are in Walden University's Health Informatics, Software Engineering, and Cyber Security Master's degree programs. I performed the research which enabled Walden University to be designated as an NSA Center in Academic Excellence in Cyber Defense in 2014. I was part of a team working closely with leadership to design and implement new master’s degree specialization in Big Data Analytics. Recently I have started helping students in the DIT program where I am the dissertation chair and committee member.\nPrior to coming to Walden University, I worked in the field of information systems and technology for over 30 years.", 'url': 'https://www.waldenu.edu/online-masters-programs/ms-in-cybersecurity', 'url_path': '/online-masters-programs/'}, {'doc_id': '1-2-chunk-1', 'source': 'walden_university', 'text': "in data science online program will be prepared to: Evaluate emerging technical developments that apply to data science. Analyze current technologies that provide practical solutions to data science problems. Explore the role of supporting technologies for data science in data-driven decision-making. Analyze legal, ethical, professional, and social issue elements within the domain of data science. Differentiate how the techniques and tools of big data predictive analytics can be used to add 'business value' in data-driven decision-making in the modern workplace. Below are some of the distinguished faculty members who bring diverse industry expertise and a passion for teaching to the Walden community. faculty name Gail Miles Program Director Dr. Miles taught Computer Science face-to-face for over 25 years starting at the University of Florida. She retired from Lenoir-Rhyne University as Professor Emerita in 2013. She taught IT online since 2000 in a variety of levels and programs. She was the Director of Online Studies for the Masters Programmes of the Department of Computer Science, University of Liverpool in the UK from 2013 to 2019. She is currently the Associate Dean of Masters programs in Information Technology, Doctor of Information Technology, PhD in Management, and Doctor of Business Administration in College of Management and Human Potential for Walden University\nAll of her graduate work was completed at the University of Florida (MEd, EdS, PhD, and MS). The second faculty name Osama Morad Contributing Faculty College of Management and Human Potential Doctor of Information Technology (DIT). Data science is the process of extracting insights from data.", 'url': 'https://www.waldenu.edu/online-masters-programs/ms-in-data-science', 'url_path': '/online-masters-programs/ms-in-data-science'}, {'doc_id': '1-0-chunk-1', 'source': 'walden_university', 'text': "You offer total 5 programs = 3 MS and 2 BS program there is the list of all programs, MS programs =  Data Science, Cybersecurity, Criminal Justice. BS programs = Bachelor’s in Business Administration, BS in Communication. Title: MS in Data Science | Walden University 