2025-04-26 00:38:57,089 - walden_rag - INFO - Data from vectore DB: '[{'doc_id': '5-0-chunk-1', 'source': '', 'text': 'Online Bachelor’s Programs\nDiscover online bachelor’s degree programs that can help advance your career .Turn Your Ambition Into Achievement With Walden Wayfinder™\nYour journey of change doesn’t have to be a solo mission. Follow Walden Wayfinder™, a guided, all-inclusive path that begins with your destination in mind. You won’t just earn your online bachelor’s degree; you’ll get a personalized, step-by-step road map to a thriving career. From exclusive tuition savings to integrated career planning from Day 1, Walden takes the guesswork out of preparing for your future. You bring your dreams and ambitions—we’ll show you the way forward. Program Variety\n\n.Transfer of Credit\n\nTransfer up to 75% of credits required for your degree program from past college courses, military service, or an associate degree.Walden Undergraduate Academy®\n\nThis dedicated online learning track offers support, tuition savings, and resources for those without previous college credit.Career Resources\n\nTake advantage of our Career Planning and Development Center for one-on-one guidance, networking events, essential job search tools, and more.Applying is Easy', 'url': 'https://www.waldenu.edu/online-bachelors-programs', 'url_path': '/online-bachelors-programs/'}, {'doc_id': '5-0-chunk-2', 'source': '', 'text': ' learning track offers support, tuition savings, and resources for those without previous college credit.Career Resources\n\nTake advantage of our Career Planning and Development Center for one-on-one guidance, networking events, essential job search tools, and more.Applying is Easy\n\nNo application fee, essay, or SAT or ACT score is required for admission. Bachelor’s Programs BS in Business Administration, BS in Communication.  An Accredited University\nQuality matters—especially when it comes to your education. Walden is accredited by The Higher Learning Commission and committed to maintaining the highest standards of excellence. Flexibility to Fit Your Schedule\nAt Walden, we are dedicated to offering education options designed to fit the needs of working professionals like you. That is why we offer a wide range of learning options, including a standard, course-based experience, and Tempo Learning®. COURSE BASED\nInstructor-led\nEngage in a course-by-course experience, where you progress on a predetermined schedule. This format allows you to learn alongside your peers, participating in weekly discussions and meeting established deadlines for assignments. Your cost is based on how many credits you need to complete your program.\n\nIdeal for students who are newer to online education and prefer structure, working with others, and having set deadlines.\n\nStarts on May 26\n\nRegister and pay by course.\n\nCourse lengths are predetermined, based on program.\n\nFaculty guide you through each course.\n\nScheduled due dates allow you make steady progress.', 'url': 'https://www.waldenu.edu/online-bachelors-programs', 'url_path': '/online-bachelors-programs/'}, {'doc_id': '1-1-chunk-1', 'source': 'walden_university', 'text': "More information for international applicants. Questions about the courses you will take? We believe you can achieve your goals and we are here to support you along your journey. Request information to learn more about scholarships and financial aid for those who apply and qualify. Walden offers tuition savings options that can make your goals more attainable. Discover savings opportunities by exploring our scholarships and grants, for those who apply and qualify. Time to completion varies by student, depending on individual progress and credits transferred, if applicable. Tuition and time to complete may be reduced if transfer credits are accepted, or if you receive grants, scholarships, or other tuition reductions. Walden may accept up to 20 transfer credits. For a personalized estimate of the number of your transfer credits that Walden would accept, call an Enrollment Specialist at844-529-2438. Books and materials are not included and may cost up to an additional $1,000 and $1,400. PROGRAM OUTCOMES Our online master's in data science program integrates core business, compliance, and management principles with the rigorous, hands-on training you need to excel in your field. Explore machine learning as you discover how to collect, analyze, and visualize an ever-growing volume of data from information systems. Learn to share insights with stakeholders to empower better decision-making. Work toward becoming the voice of data responsibility and the go-to data expert in your organization and beyond. Career Outlook Now more than ever, businesses need data scientists to help them interpret and leverage a growing volume of raw data. An online data science degree program can help provide you with the hands-on training and specialized technical knowledge necessary to fill this pressing need.", 'url': 'https://www.waldenu.edu/online-masters-programs/ms-in-data-science', 'url_path': '/online-masters-programs/ms-in-data-science'}, {'doc_id': '3-2-chunk-3', 'source': 'walden_university', 'text': "uhainy, B. (2021). Ways to Bloom Where You’re Planted. Information Security Professional ISC2\n\nPresentations\nDUHAINY, B. (2022). Cybersecurity Attacks and Countermeasures . FBI Citizens Academy\n\nDuhainy, B. (2022). Infrastructure Security. FBI Citizens Academy Duhainy, B. (2020). Cybersecurity in the age of AI, Automation and GDPR. Walden University. Gary Griffith\nAcademic Coordinator  \nCollege of Management and Human Potential\nDoctor of Business Administration (DBA)   Dr. Gary Griffith started teaching as a contributing faculty for Walden University in the Master of Science in Information Systems Management program in 2011. In 2012 I accepted a core faculty position in the Master of Science in Information Technology program. Since starting my career at Walden University I have taught 16 different courses in BSIT, MISM, MSIT and DIT programs. Most of the courses I teach are in Walden University's Health Informatics, Software Engineering, and Cyber Security Master's degree programs. I performed the research which enabled Walden University to be designated as an NSA Center in Academic Excellence in Cyber Defense in 2014. I was part of a team working closely with leadership to design and implement new master’s degree specialization in Big Data Analytics. Recently I have started helping students in the DIT program where I am the dissertation chair and committee member.\nPrior to coming to Walden University, I worked in the field of information systems and technology for over 30 years.", 'url': 'https://www.waldenu.edu/online-masters-programs/ms-in-cybersecurity', 'url_path': '/online-masters-programs/'}, {'doc_id': '6-0-chunk-3', 'source': '', 'text': ' the admissions process. Start your journey with:\n\nNo application fee\n\nEasy credit transfer\n\nNo essay.  Admission Criteria = Admission is considered for adult students who hold a high school diploma or its equivalent. Applicants must also meet one of the following criteria:\n\nYou are 21 years of age or older.\nYou are less than 21 years of age with at least 12 quarter credits.\nYou are an active member of the military or a veteran with documentation of service. Choose Your Concentration\nChoose from eight BS in Business Administration concentrations to focus on the career and future you want. Accounting,Finance,General Program,Healthcare Management,Human Resource Management,Management,Marketing,Small Business Management.  tuition and fees : Tuition Breakdown\nWe know cost is a major consideration when exploring online BS in Business Administration programs. That’s why Walden offers opportunities to reduce your tuition through:\n\nExperience-based credits\n\nSpecial tuition savings\n\nBelieve & Achieve Scholarship. General Program Concentration Course-Based Learning = Curriculum Component\tRequirements\tCost\tAmount\nTuition\t181 quarter credit hours\t$350 per quarter hour\t\n$63,350\n\nProgram Fee\tPer quarter\t$180\t\n$2,880\n\n$66,230**\n\nBELIEVE & ACHIEVE SCHOLARSHIP\n\nYOUR TUITION\t\n-$19,250\n\n$46,980*\n\n. Books and materials are not included and may cost up to an additional $5,500. Tempo Learning = Progress at Your Pace. Control Your Cost.\n\nWalden’s Tempo Learning® programs follow a subscription-based pricing format. Students are billed a flat-rate for each 3-month subscription term. All pricing is represented in U.S. dollars and is subject to change.', 'url': 'https://www.waldenu.edu/online-bachelors-programs/bs-in-business-administration', 'url_path': '/online-bachelors-programs/'}]' >>>>>>>>>>>>>>
